# AGENTS.md

This folder holds the charts for {{ project_name }}, built with the mozaic chart library
(Svelte 5 + d3) as static embeds. House style: `src/lib/theme.ts`{% if outlet != 'none' %} ({{ 'SAMIZDATA' if outlet == 'samizdata' else 'Ziarul de Gardă' }}){% endif %}.
Languages: see `mozaic.config.ts`.

## Where things go

- Data wrangling stays in the project's `etl/` scripts and `docs/` notebooks. Write the tidy CSV each chart
  needs to `charts/data/` (committed; `data/processed/` is not).
- Charts: `src/charts/<slug>/` with `Chart.svelte` (the chart), `data.ts` (load and type the
  CSV), `messages.ts` (every user-facing string, per language). Register in `src/charts/index.ts`.
- Do not edit `src/routes/embed/**`, `manifest.json` or `embed.js` routes; they are generic.
{%- if outlet != 'none' %}
- Do not edit `src/lib/brands/`: it is a copy of the outlet's brand, updated by `copier update`.
{%- endif %}
- Publishing: `../.github/workflows/charts.yml` builds this folder and deploys `build/` to GitHub
  Pages on every push to `main` that changes `charts/`. Set `baseUrl` in `mozaic.config.ts`.
{%- if mozaic_path %}
- mozaic is linked from `{{ mozaic_path }}`. A missing mark or option belongs in the library
  there (with a test and a gallery example), not in this project; run `pnpm --filter mozaic package` after changing it.
{%- endif %}

## Chart conventions

- Wrap everything in `<Chart {style} {locale} {medium} {width} alt="…">` with `Header`
  (`Title`, `Subtitle`), a `Plot`, and `Footer` (`Notes`, `Source`).
- Scales are plain d3 scales. Set the domain; `<Plot>` sets the range.
- Draw in `<Svg>`; tooltips go in `<Html>`. Use {% raw %}`{#snippet children(plot)}`{% endraw %} on `<Plot>`
  to get ranged scales for tooltip positions.
- Colours: `style.palettes` (the theme each chart receives); assign categorical colours by
  entity in order. Text uses text colours (`var(--mz-color-text)`), never data colours.
- Every chart needs `alt` text, a legend for 2+ series, and strings in every language.
- Use the theme's breakpoints (`plot.breakpoint`) for small-screen layouts.
- Name the y unit once, on the top tick: `<AxisY unit="lei/m³" />`.
- Tooltips: `<Tooltip title items>`, one item per series (label, value, colour), so values line up.
- Event markers on a time axis: `<RefLine x={date} label="…" dotted labelY={-30} />`, labels above the plot.
- Link each source to its data or document: `<Source sources={[{ label: 'ANRE', href: '…' }, …]} />`
  (recipes take the same list as `source`).
- No `<DataTable>` ("Show the data" button) unless asked for.

## Before you finish

- `pnpm check` passes.
- Look at the preview (`pnpm dev`) at 320 px and 1000 px, in every language, and in print medium.
- `pnpm build` succeeds.

The full component reference and examples are in the mozaic docs site (the library's `apps/docs`).
